# ==============================================================================
# GitHub Linguist Configuration for Dependencies
# ==============================================================================
# This section configures how GitHub treats third-party dependencies in the 
# `libs/` folder (which are tracked as git subtrees).
#
# By explicitly listing each dependency and applying the following flags:
#  - `linguist-vendored`: Excludes the dependency from the repository's 
#    overall language statistics (e.g., stops C++ stats from being skewed).
#  - `linguist-generated`: Forces GitHub to collapse these files by default 
#    in Pull Request diffs, saving reviewers from scrolling through third-party code.
#
# IMPORTANT: 
# We specify each dependency directory individually rather than using `libs/*`. 
# This ensures that our first-party files located inside `libs/` 
# (such as `fake-dlclose/`, `patches/`, and `CMakeLists.txt`) are NOT collapsed 
# or ignored, ensuring they remain fully visible and reviewable in Pull Requests.
# ==============================================================================

libs/ALL/**        linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/antlr4/**     linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/benchmark/**  linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/eigen/**      linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/googletest/** linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/harmony/**    linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/highway/**    linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/pmt/**        linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/spdlog/**     linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/utfcpp/**     linguist-vendored linguist-generated
libs/yaml-cpp/**   linguist-vendored linguist-generated